id: query-options
title: Mutation Options
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One of the best ways to share mutation options between multiple places,\nis to use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mutationOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" helper. At runtime, this helper just returns whatever you pass into it,\nbut it has a lot of advantages when using it "},{"type":"link","href":"../typescript.md#typing-query-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"with TypeScript"}]},{"type":"text","value":".\nYou can define all possible options for a mutation in one place,\nand you'll also get type inference and type safety for all of them."}]},{"type":"code","value":"export class QueriesService {\n  private readonly http = inject(HttpClient)\n\n  updatePost(id: number) {\n    return mutationOptions({\n      mutationFn: (post: Post) => Promise.resolve(post),\n      mutationKey: ['updatePost', id],\n      onSuccess: (newPost) => {\n        //           ^? newPost: Post\n        this.queryClient.setQueryData(['posts', id], newPost)\n      },\n    })\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nOne of the best ways to share mutation options between multiple places,\nis to use the `mutationOptions` helper. At runtime, this helper just returns whatever you pass into it,\nbut it has a lot of advantages when using it [with TypeScript](../typescript.md#typing-query-options).\nYou can define all possible options for a mutation in one place,\nand you'll also get type inference and type safety for all of them.\n\n```ts\nexport class QueriesService {\n  private readonly http = inject(HttpClient)\n\n  updatePost(id: number) {\n    return mutationOptions({\n      mutationFn: (post: Post) => Promise.resolve(post),\n      mutationKey: ['updatePost', id],\n      onSuccess: (newPost) => {\n        //           ^? newPost: Post\n        this.queryClient.setQueryData(['posts', id], newPost)\n      },\n    })\n  }\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: query-options\ntitle: Mutation Options\n---\n\nOne of the best ways to share mutation options between multiple places,\nis to use the `mutationOptions` helper. At runtime, this helper just returns whatever you pass into it,\nbut it has a lot of advantages when using it [with TypeScript](../typescript.md#typing-query-options).\nYou can define all possible options for a mutation in one place,\nand you'll also get type inference and type safety for all of them.\n\n```ts\nexport class QueriesService {\n  private readonly http = inject(HttpClient)\n\n  updatePost(id: number) {\n    return mutationOptions({\n      mutationFn: (post: Post) => Promise.resolve(post),\n      mutationKey: ['updatePost', id],\n      onSuccess: (newPost) => {\n        //           ^? newPost: Post\n        this.queryClient.setQueryData(['posts', id], newPost)\n      },\n    })\n  }\n}\n```\n"}
